  "task_text": " Review\n6/4 XP\nProperties of Transformed Logarithmic Functions\nCompleted @ 5:53 PM\nPREREQUISITES\n Solving Logarithmic Equations Containing the Natural Logarithm\n Combining Graph Transformations of Logarithmic Functions\n Further Solving Linear Inequalities\n1.The Range of a Transformed Logarithmic Function\n?\n\nFind the minimum value of \n𝑓\n(\n𝑥\n)\n=\n2\nln\n⁡\n(\n𝑥\n−\n2\n)\n+\n3.\n\nMFri, Sep 18th @ 5:49 PM|Elapsed: 3:26\nCorrect\n2.The Root of a Transformed Logarithmic Function\n?\n\nFind the root of \n𝑓\n(\n𝑥\n)\n=\nlog\n4\n⁡\n(\n3\n𝑥\n+\n1\n)\n−\n2.\n\nMFri, Sep 18th @ 5:52 PM|Elapsed: 2:06\nCorrect\n3.The Vertical Asymptote of a Transformed Logarithmic Function\n?\n\nFind the equation of the vertical asymptote of the function \n𝑓\n(\n𝑥\n)\n=\nlog\n3\n⁡\n(\n4\n𝑥\n+\n1\n)\n.\n\nEFri, Sep 18th @ 5:53 PM|Elapsed: 1:07\nCorrect",
